WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.419
I invite you to join the discussion on the
David Pakman show.

00:00:03.419 --> 00:00:08.330
Read it at David Pakman dot com slash our
a._d._d I-T.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.919
More than 19000 of you have already done that.

00:00:11.919 --> 00:00:14.719
A few interesting posts I spotted.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:20.349
One is about the suicide rate that Donald
Trump has been talking about lately, asking

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:26.400
why does no one ever question Trump on the
high suicide rate, falling life expectancy

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.640
and rising opioid usage before Cauvin 19 whenever
he brings them up as a reason to reopen the

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.640
country?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.530
Yeah, this is a very fair question.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.780
We are being Gaslight Daily by Donald Trump.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:44.340
When Donald Trump pulls out a piece of paper
from his suit jacket with a graph of the just

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:49.210
number of tests that the United States has
done, we are being gasoline, right?

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.519
We are a country of three hundred and thirty
one million people.

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:53.379
And what matters is the per capita testing
rate.

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:57.940
When Donald Trump now says, listen, staying
home can make people depressed, people could

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.790
commit suicide, people are addicted to drugs.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:05.030
These are things Donald Trump has not indicated
he ever cared about before, and they were

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.030
problems before.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.560
So you're completely right to point out the
cynical nature of that.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.250
And I wish Donald Trump were asked about it.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.520
But, you know, he would just lie and move
on to the next question.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:22.270
Another user says reminds us that Justice
Ruth Bader Ginsburg is in the hospital with

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:26.310
an infection, which is not good news.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:32.690
And I want to just take this as an opportunity
to remind everybody that we want Justice Ruth

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:38.320
Bader Ginsburg to recover and we wish her
the best and we want her to stay on the court.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.500
She says she wants to be honored until she's
90 and we want her to be able to do that.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.909
And that's absolutely fantastic.

00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:45.920
And we love her.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:51.829
And it reminds us of the fact that there is
an a level of dread that we experience when

00:01:51.829 --> 00:01:56.930
we hear that she's in the hospital and we
know that Donald Trump is president and gets

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.909
to pick Supreme Court justices.

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:06.789
Just a reminder about the importance of who
is allowed to select the next Supreme Court

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:07.789
justice.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:08.970
Very, very important.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:15.450
Lastly, a post on our subreddit from user
John Ex Wall, who says, how can you prove

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.630
you are not a sexual assaulter?

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:19.920
I don't know the answer to this.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.450
I think that this is something that needs
to be discussed.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:27.670
And you all know my positions on on allegations
of sexual assault.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:32.080
I believe that as a general rule, these need
to be taken seriously.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.750
They need to be investigated.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:40.140
We need to ensure that men or women who are
victims of sexual assault are not dissuaded

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:46.100
from coming forward because of how they expect
to be treated or shame or whatever else.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:51.700
I don't know how you prove that you didn't
sexually assault someone when there is not

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.830
a criminal proceeding.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:58.800
I think that many of us, if there is actually
a criminal trial about rape, for example,

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.460
and the individual is found not guilty, of
course, we all know you can be found not guilty

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:08.420
and have actually done the thing you were
accused of, but legally be not guilty.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:12.460
But I believe that there is more of a sense
that when you're found not guilty of rape,

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:17.030
you didn't do it, even though, of course,
that that's not always the case when you have

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:23.360
an allegation that never gets to a police
report or a criminal proceeding and the accused

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.730
perpetrator denies it.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.940
I don't know how you prove you didn't do it.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.250
I really don't.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.210
And I don't even have anything to add.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:35.520
I would leave it to you to give me some thoughts
about that.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.010
Join these discussions at David Pakman dot
com slash.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:38.360
Read it.

